From: prplMesh virtual-radio lab
Subject: [PATCH] platform: map the configured third Linux radio

The native Linux build already exposes BEEROCKS_WLAN3_IFACE and emits
wlan4 hostapd/supplicant paths in the platform database. The Linux BPL
helper nevertheless rejects radio number 2, preventing the otherwise
configured third radio from being instantiated.

--- a/framework/platform/bpl/cfg/linux/bpl_cfg_ifaces.cpp.in
+++ b/framework/platform/bpl/cfg/linux/bpl_cfg_ifaces.cpp.in
@@ -31,6 +31,7 @@ bool radio_num_to_wlan_iface_name(const int32_t radio_num, std::string& iface_s
     switch (radio_num) {
         case 0: iface_str = "@BEEROCKS_WLAN1_IFACE@"; break;
         case 1: iface_str = "@BEEROCKS_WLAN2_IFACE@"; break;
+        case 2: iface_str = "@BEEROCKS_WLAN3_IFACE@"; break;
         default:
             return false;
     }
